{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774134493,"nonce":"f2n7MPqd95A3iysPQuhMAf2pnZg=","title":"Dev-browser queue: concurrent agent browser verification without interference","message":"When multiple agents need to use dev-browser (Playwright) for UI verification, they currently risk interfering with each other (navigating the same page, modifying state). A queueing system would let agents submit verification requests that execute serially.\n\nPossible approaches:\n- Queue with blocking wait from the agents perspective (submit, wait for result)\n- Multiple browser contexts/profiles that cant interfere\n- Named page isolation (dev-browser already supports named pages)\n\nMANDATORY RESEARCH NOTE: Before implementing, the assigned agent MUST research whether this problem can be obviated entirely — e.g., by using dev-browsers existing named page feature with separate browser contexts, or by using Playwrights built-in browser context isolation. If the problem is already solvable without a queue, document that finding and notify the user. Only build a queue if isolation alone is insufficient.\n\nThis is high-value for parallel agent engineering workflows.","files":null}]}